        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(session-memory): use shortenHomePath for safe home-path display in logs",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`saveSessionMemoryNow` in `src/hooks/bundled/session-memory/handler.ts` uses `memoryFilePath.replace(os.homedir(), \"~\")` at two call sites to shorten home paths in log output. `String.replace()` is unbounded and corrupts sibling paths that happen to share the home prefix as a substring.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace with the existing `shortenHomePath()` utility from `src/utils.ts`, which checks `startsWith(\"${home}/\")` boundaries. This is a one-line swap at each call site and the utility is already available in the import graph.\n\n## User Impact\n\nLog messages from the session-memory hook show corrupted paths when the user has a sibling directory sharing the home prefix (e.g., `/home/user` vs `/home/user2`).\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Real behavior proof — reproduced via node:**\n```\nInput:  \"/home/user2/.openclaw/state/memory/test.md\" (home=/home/user)\nOLD:    \"~2/.openclaw/state/memory/test.md\"  <- corrupted\nNEW:    \"/home/user2/.openclaw/state/memory/test.md\"  <- preserved\n```\n\n**Validation:**\n- tsgo typecheck: passed\n- `pnpm test src/hooks/bundled/session-memory/handler.test.ts`: 29 tests passed\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
